; The floor of the melange work, on its own alias.
;
; @melange builds the probe and needs the jsont patch to apply.
; @melange-scaffold needs only the Bigarray shim, fmt, and jsont_base -- the
; parts that hold regardless -- so there is always a melange target that
; builds, and CI never has to point at something expected to fail.
;
; A real melange.emit rather than a bare alias with file dependencies: linking
; through the normal stanza is what actually proves the libraries are usable,
; and it avoids depending on dune's private .objs/melange layout.

(melange.emit
 (target output)
 (alias melange-scaffold)
 (module_systems commonjs)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{profile} melange))
 (modules scaffold)
 (libraries bigarray_mel fmt_mel jsont_base_mel))
